and so, that contributed to it,

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.210
not being as good of a vacation

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.160
as vacations used to be before COVID,

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.430
but the main thing that happened to me...

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:33.030
Yeah, that can bring you to a four,

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:34.070
because just being,

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:38.080
I mean, we're blessed to be
able to go on a vacation.

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:39.221
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:39.221 --> 00:10:40.800
And we know that.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:45.060
But the thing is is that I have a problem,

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:46.540
I've talked about it before,

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.300
and I think this is pretty common.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:51.750
People you tie expectations to things,

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.480
whether it's a vacation,
a project, whatever,

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:57.542
but vacations are the
things that most people tie

00:10:57.542 --> 00:10:59.700
a certain level of expectation to,

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.920
and you think about it
and you fool yourself

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.220
into thinking that like,

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:05.669
oh, but when I go on vacation,

00:11:05.669 --> 00:11:07.491
that's gonna be a great week.

00:11:07.491 --> 00:11:10.855
Like, oh, that vacation week at the beach,

00:11:10.855 --> 00:11:12.820
man, that's gonna be good.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.400
'Cause that's the point of it.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.160
And then I started thinking things like

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:21.160
well, what am I gonna do on the vacation,

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:23.383
'cause I wanna make sure

00:11:23.383 --> 00:11:26.280
that I'm doing the vacation well, right?

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.397
And so then my sort of expectation was,

00:11:29.397 --> 00:11:31.890
and first of all, I'm a lot
more aware of this than I was,

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:33.590
say 10, 20 years ago,

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.970
where I unconsciously went into situations

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:38.640
with all these expectations
and then I was disappointed.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.160
At least I had gotten to a point

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:43.980
where I know the way my mind works is

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:45.370
you have these expectations,

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:46.790
you need to set low expectations,

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:47.700
you need to go with the flow,

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.500
but I just find myself
getting to the place

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.430
where I've still got the expectations,

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:53.072
and the expectations of this vacation were

00:11:53.072 --> 00:11:58.072
I want to actually get a
lot of surf time in, right?

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:01.903
I wanna surf, but I also
wanna get my kids surfing,

00:12:01.903 --> 00:12:03.590
pretty much for the first time,

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:05.436
locking down a little bit
earlier in the summer.

00:12:05.436 --> 00:12:10.436
And, me and you stand
up paddleboard, surf,

00:12:11.112 --> 00:12:14.592
and I've had this secret
hope to be able to...

00:12:14.592 --> 00:12:15.425
You don't believe that counts.

00:12:15.425 --> 00:12:17.750
To regular... well, the thing is is that

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:20.150
there's lots of places in
the world that if you go

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:23.330
and you didn't bring your
big ass paddleboard with you,

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:25.480
you don't have an option to surf,

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:27.342
and then there's also a
lot of really cool breaks

00:12:27.342 --> 00:12:31.040
where you're not really supposed to be,

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.680
you're not even allowed to
be on a stand-up paddleboard

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:34.600
in some places.

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:36.150
So I was just like, I would
just like to have that in

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:39.210
my arsenal of abilities,
the ability to like surf,

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:42.480
and I'm not talking about like hang ten,

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.610
or catch big, I'm talking
like old man on a long board,

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:48.010
like just the bare
minimum, catching the wave.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:50.150
I get that, you want the versatility.

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:52.028
So I was like, okay, San Diego,

00:12:52.028 --> 00:12:55.905
it's an easier surf town,

00:12:55.905 --> 00:13:00.140
we were on various beaches
between LA and San Diego,

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:02.020
but we were closer to San Diego,

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:04.243
and it's just easier to surf down there,

00:13:04.243 --> 00:13:06.100
it's less territorial,

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:08.650
there's more places to surf,
there's less people, whatever.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.710
So I was super excited about that,

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:12.710
and we were like walking
distance from a place that

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:14.966
was like a good place to learn.

00:13:14.966 --> 00:13:19.966
And I took my long board
that I bought this year

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:24.150
down there.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:27.770
And day one, I go out,
and it's frustrating,

00:13:30.759 --> 00:13:34.140
it's frustrating when you
know that you could be

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:36.510
already standing up on a
paddleboard and surfing.

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:37.680
Yep.

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:40.620
But you're sitting there,
trying to stand up,

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.650
and like not balancing,
falling off the board.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:46.680
Yeah, it kinda reminds me
when we decided to start

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:51.041
snow skiing even though we
were both pretty decent at

00:13:51.041 --> 00:13:52.080
snowboarding.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.680
Exactly, like I know how to do this.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:57.148
You have to invest like a whole ski trip

00:13:57.148 --> 00:13:59.260
just to learn how to do something

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:00.780
when you could be enjoying
it doing the thing

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:01.760
you already know how to do.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:02.700
Right.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:04.550
So, day one was pretty frustrating.

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:06.410
There were a couple of moments of hope.

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:08.890
And the reason you ski is 'cause

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:11.140
as you get older, it's
like it's better on your...

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.430
Well, it's harder on your
knees, easier on your back,

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:14.263
for me.

00:14:14.263 --> 00:14:15.870
That's why I transitioned to skiing.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.800
It's not good on the pelvis.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.910
And that's why I transitioned
to stand up paddle boarding

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:22.910
'cause it's easier on the back for me.

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:25.230
Case in point, day two, I go out,

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:30.010
and I don't know exactly what is going on,

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:32.354
but one of the things that
has always happened to me,

00:14:32.354 --> 00:14:36.820
it used to happen before
I would go on a vacation,

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:38.780
or before there was a
significant transition,

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:40.403
or in the midst of a transition.

00:14:40.403 --> 00:14:43.489
I would have my lower back act up

00:14:43.489 --> 00:14:45.300
and basically...

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:46.310
Your back would go out.

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:48.610
Go back to what I call
my ground zero injury,

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.960
which is related to my herniated disc,

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:53.460
it's in a very specific spot
in the left side of my spine

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:56.925
and then, you know, 10 years
ago, when this would happen,

00:14:56.925 --> 00:14:59.370
even five years ago,
when this would happen,

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:02.270
I would be out, I would
be in pain for months

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:03.430
when this happened.

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:05.280
Now I've gotten to a place
where I can experience

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:06.113
that injury

00:15:06.113 --> 00:15:08.070
and then a few days later I'm
pretty functional or whatever

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:09.810
and now, a week later,
as I'm about to tell you,

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:11.586
I did hurt my back.

00:15:11.586 --> 00:15:16.586
But, the second day, I
wake up, and first of all,

00:15:17.287 --> 00:15:22.287
the X factor of any
vacation is the bed, right?

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:24.460
What is this bed gonna
be like in this AirBnB?

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:26.520
When you got a bad back,
you're very sensitive

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:28.113
to beds in general

00:15:28.113 --> 00:15:31.690
and the softer the bed, the
worse it is on your back.

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:34.497
That's the case for a lot of
people with back problems.

00:15:34.497 --> 00:15:38.680
I was like, man, this bed
is unnecessarily soft.

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:42.146
I love a soft bed, my bed was too hard.

00:15:42.146 --> 00:15:43.840
We should've swapped.

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:45.634
I almost slept on the floor

00:15:45.634 --> 00:15:48.997
for most of the time, but I didn't,

00:15:48.997 --> 00:15:51.190
there was a mattress
topper, I took that off

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:54.353
after the second night,
but got up that second day

00:15:54.353 --> 00:15:56.010
and was like, man, my back is tight,

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:59.240
but I did all my stuff
that I do to loosen up.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:03.460
Locke and I go down to
the beach and second wave

00:16:04.593 --> 00:16:09.593
standing up, and I feel
like oh, there it is,

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:14.798
oh no, oh no, oh no, and
it's like a sharp pain,

00:16:14.798 --> 00:16:18.430
but then I'm like, okay,
but no, I'm in better shape,

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:21.446
let me just go in, I'm gonna
do some stretches on the beach,

00:16:21.446 --> 00:16:23.370
like an old man.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:26.141
So you rode two waves, and the second one.

00:16:26.141 --> 00:16:28.590
Well, I didn't ride the
wave, I was in the process

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:30.650
of standing up when it went out on me.

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:32.580
And then you fell over.

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:36.690
And then I swim in to the
beach, I get on the beach,

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:38.320
I do my stuff,

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:41.428
and then it hits me very,
very squarely and clearly,

00:16:41.428 --> 00:16:44.130
you're not going back out today.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:47.690
And so, I like wave at Locke
and I'm like I gotta go in.

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:51.120
He was like, okay, and he
stays out there by himself.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:53.550
I walk back to the
house, carrying my board,

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:54.510
which is not feeling great,

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:58.400
because I gotta walk
like a quarter mile or so

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.430
with this board, my back is hurting.

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:03.676
'Cause standing up on a...
it's an explosive act.

00:17:03.676 --> 00:17:05.030
Yeah.

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:08.750
To go from paddling on your
chest to like standing up

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:09.600
on a board.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.200
I was trying to show
Lincoln how to do that

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:12.730
'cause there were foam
boards that happened to be

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:13.720
at the place we stayed,

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:14.830
'cause I don't own any of those,

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:19.750
'cause, I didn't wanna
make that transition,

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:21.130
but I'm like, hey, it's here,

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:22.610
and I'm showing him on the beach

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:26.954
how to stand up, and it's explosive,

00:17:26.954 --> 00:17:30.147
and there's twisting involved too.

00:17:30.147 --> 00:17:33.793
You're supposed to be turning your hips.

00:17:34.822 --> 00:17:36.550
I don't know, I can imagine
that it can really...

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.060
Well, but here's the thing...

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:39.550
Wring your back.

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:42.090
And you know, I was talking
about this in therapy

00:17:42.090 --> 00:17:42.923
because...

00:17:42.923 --> 00:17:44.370
Physical therapy?

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.932
I do,

00:17:46.932 --> 00:17:49.670
I don't wanna get into too much woo,

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:52.230
and I don't know exactly
what I think about this,

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:54.130
but I do know that there's a connection

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:57.870
to emotional sort of pain and stress

00:17:57.870 --> 00:17:59.720
that manifests itself physically

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.620
in ways that we don't quite understand.

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:02.830
Okay.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:05.220
This has just been
proven many, many times.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:07.570
Like, I told you, every
time I get ready to

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:09.598
go on vacation or I'm in
the midst of a vacation,

00:18:09.598 --> 00:18:12.870
there are many years where my back would,

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:15.170
I could just feel it tensing up, right?

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:17.300
'Cause it's like the act of relaxing,

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:19.390
and it's very difficult for me to relax

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:20.465
on vacation.

00:18:20.465 --> 00:18:22.865
I'll talk about a little
bit more lately, later.

00:18:25.136 --> 00:18:29.805
And so I think the act of
trying to relax a little bit,

00:18:29.805 --> 00:18:33.960
plus the bed, plus the
act of doing something,

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:36.380
I don't know exactly what
the pie chart is that

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:39.418
contributed to it, but
it was the perfect storm.

00:18:39.418 --> 00:18:43.980
But all that to say I was
immediately deflated, right?

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:47.250
And it felt like, 'cause I was like...

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:48.870
Can't surf the rest of the week.

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:52.780
I was like am I gonna be able
to surf paddle board at all?

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:54.592
I'm not gonna be able to surf at all

00:18:54.592 --> 00:18:58.048
for the rest of the week, and this is,

00:18:58.048 --> 00:19:02.011
a very privileged problem,

00:19:02.011 --> 00:19:06.330
but also I was upset because the AirBnB,

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.930
which came with a hot tub,

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:09.620
the hot tub wasn't working
and they were like,

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:11.940
we can't fix it while you're there.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:14.130
Because the manufacturer said it's broken,

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.730
it has to be replaced or something.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:16.577
So I was like, oh, I hurt my back

00:19:16.577 --> 00:19:18.760
and I also can't get into
the hot tub to make myself

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:19.970
feel better.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:20.803
Wah, wah!

00:19:22.091 --> 00:19:24.150
So that's a four, you plummeted.

00:19:24.150 --> 00:19:25.405
Yeah, and I was like...

00:19:25.405 --> 00:19:26.612
Or is that lower than a four?

00:19:26.612 --> 00:19:30.560
No, well, okay, so when it happened to me,

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.840
as I was walking back to the house

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:35.710
thinking about the fact
that my expectations

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:37.381
had been thwarted, I was like,

00:19:37.381 --> 00:19:40.620
of course this is what
has happened, right?

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:41.984
Because.

00:19:41.984 --> 00:19:44.127
What do you mean?

00:19:44.127 --> 00:19:46.030
'Cause you think you deserve it?

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:47.290
You deserve to be punished?

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.190
No, no, it's not about being deserving,

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:53.190
it's just like this is the
perfect gift from the universe

00:19:53.547 --> 00:19:58.010
for someone who is bringing
this level of expectations.

00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:00.270
If what you really want to learn how to do

00:20:00.270 --> 00:20:03.290
is to accept things, to go with the flow,

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:06.450
to not have all of these
expectations tied up

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:07.970
in your experiences,

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:10.110
but to let things happen to you,

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:11.257
to let things come to you,

00:20:11.257 --> 00:20:13.291
'cause even when I'm out there surfing,

00:20:13.291 --> 00:20:17.670
it's very difficult for me to have fun,

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:20.670
because I'm focused on doing it well,

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:21.503
you know what I'm saying?

00:20:21.503 --> 00:20:23.640
I'm like, you gotta get up
and you gotta catch this wave,

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:27.290
it's like I approach it
like an athletic event

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:30.060
versus like an enjoyable thing

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.560
'cause there's this part
of me that's just like,

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.230
you gotta get good enough at this

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:35.160
before you can enjoy it.

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:36.700
If you get good enough at it,

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:39.060
then you can actually sit
back and reap the benefits

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:40.727
of the joy that comes from it.

00:20:40.727 --> 00:20:45.727
So long story short is
my back got better enough

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:49.607
to stand up paddle
board, the very last day,

00:20:49.607 --> 00:20:52.177
I had a really good surfing day,

00:20:52.177 --> 00:20:53.950
caught a bunch of waves,

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:56.159
it kinda redeemed the experience,

00:20:56.159 --> 00:21:01.159
but the fact that my expectations
were kinda ripped apart,

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.540
I didn't learn how to do regular surfing,

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:06.950
I wasn't able to surf,
even on a paddle board

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:09.030
for two days after I hurt my back.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:12.730
It was almost like the
vacation was a lesson.

00:21:12.730 --> 00:21:14.670
And lessons aren't fun,

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:17.104
so it wasn't like, oh, I'm
having an incredible time

00:21:17.104 --> 00:21:20.670
doing the thing that I
thought I was gonna do,

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.860
I'm really just kinda sitting here wishing

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:25.170
that I was doing the thing
that I thought I was gonna do.

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:27.470
It's interesting you
say lessons aren't fun,

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.440
but do you think that you would
have enjoyed your vacation

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:33.770
more if you didn't see it as a lesson,

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:35.810
that you just said, oh, I have an injury,

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:38.062
now I gotta pivot to just
watching Netflix the whole time

00:21:38.062 --> 00:21:39.540
I'm here?

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:42.690
Well, I'll talk about that later.

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:46.260
'Cause that is what I did, and
that created another sort of

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:48.770
weird emotional experience to it.

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:50.540
Okay, dang, man.

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:52.137
I'm very in touch with myself.

00:21:52.137 --> 00:21:55.109
But seeing it as a lesson,

00:21:55.109 --> 00:21:57.550
you said lessons aren't fun,

00:21:57.550 --> 00:22:00.710
but I actually think that this mindset

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:03.491
of accepting what happened to you

00:22:03.491 --> 00:22:06.069
as something to learn from,

00:22:06.069 --> 00:22:09.710
didn't that help redeem it a little bit?

00:22:09.710 --> 00:22:11.489
Yeah, yeah, it did, but it wasn't...

00:22:11.489 --> 00:22:16.489
It wasn't fun in a recreational sense,

00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:18.520
but it was valuable.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:19.570
It's like the process,

00:22:19.570 --> 00:22:23.460
I was reading this book where the woman

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:26.363
was talking about the process
of sort of transformation

00:22:26.363 --> 00:22:31.106
that takes place in people
who are trying to change

00:22:31.106 --> 00:22:34.530
and the process of change,

00:22:34.530 --> 00:22:36.984
she uses the analogy of like leather,

00:22:36.984 --> 00:22:37.850
you know?

00:22:37.850 --> 00:22:38.880
Tanning a hide.

00:22:38.880 --> 00:22:39.713
Okay.

00:22:39.713 --> 00:22:42.102
And like, you know, at
first it's just really hard,

00:22:42.102 --> 00:22:47.102
it's not pliable at all,
it's like a big potato chip.

00:22:47.230 --> 00:22:49.440
It's like raw hide, like
what you would give your dog

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:50.452
to eat.

00:22:50.452 --> 00:22:52.770
But the process of tanning and stretching

00:22:52.770 --> 00:22:55.300
and hanging it up, I don't
know what happens to leather,

00:22:55.300 --> 00:22:57.360
but eventually it becomes nice and supple

00:22:57.360 --> 00:23:00.109
but if you imagine yourself as this hide,

00:23:00.109 --> 00:23:02.100
going through that process,

00:23:02.100 --> 00:23:03.970
you're being stretched
and you're in the sun,

00:23:03.970 --> 00:23:07.570
it's not fun, but you're
becoming what you're supposed

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:09.780
to be becoming, and I
know that's not what they,

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:11.648
again, that's not what they...

00:23:11.648 --> 00:23:12.481
A seat for a cowboy's crotch.

00:23:12.481 --> 00:23:13.863
That's not what vacation is,

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:19.830
vacation is traditionally
like a break from the norm,

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:22.390
it's a time to relax, it's a time to,

00:23:22.390 --> 00:23:25.840
when you live, yeah, we
have an incredible job,

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:26.673
we're living the dream,

00:23:26.673 --> 00:23:28.877
but it's very busy and
there's constantly things

00:23:28.877 --> 00:23:30.798
we have to engage with.

00:23:30.798 --> 00:23:33.399
Trying to disengage,
which is difficult for me,

00:23:33.399 --> 00:23:37.250
for me it was just that
lesson of not getting

00:23:37.250 --> 00:23:38.844
what you thought you wanted

00:23:38.844 --> 00:23:41.769
but getting what you actually needed.

00:23:41.769 --> 00:23:44.911
I'm just saying, when
you asked that question,

00:23:44.911 --> 00:23:49.630
on a scale of one to 10, I'm
thinking the enjoyment factor,

00:23:49.630 --> 00:23:51.850
maybe the long term
value of it, it's a 10,

00:23:51.850 --> 00:23:53.957
versus if I had gone down
there and learned how to surf

00:23:53.957 --> 00:23:56.550
and it was awesome it would've
been a one in the long term

00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:57.797
value.

00:23:57.797 --> 00:24:00.590
But once the injury happened,
seeing it through the lens

00:24:00.590 --> 00:24:03.173
of how can I grow here,

00:24:03.173 --> 00:24:04.170
it helps.

00:24:04.170 --> 00:24:05.003
Redeemed it.

00:24:05.003 --> 00:24:06.574
I mean...

00:24:06.574 --> 00:24:08.112
It redeemed it, but the
lesson wasn't enjoyable.

00:24:08.112 --> 00:24:10.360
Okay.

00:24:10.360 --> 00:24:11.330
'Cause everyday I was like,

00:24:11.330 --> 00:24:12.893
man, I wish I was surfing right now

00:24:12.893 --> 00:24:16.050
and thinking that oh, even when I do surf,

00:24:16.050 --> 00:24:17.460
I'm gonna have to be on
the stand up paddle board,

00:24:17.460 --> 00:24:18.920
I already know how to do that,

00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:20.330
that's no fun,

00:24:20.330 --> 00:24:21.163
you know what I'm saying?

00:24:21.163 --> 00:24:22.020
That's how I was thinking about it.

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:24.060
Ironically that's when it should be fun,

00:24:24.060 --> 00:24:25.350
'cause that's what you said earlier.

00:24:25.350 --> 00:24:27.510
Right.
That when you know how to...

00:24:27.510 --> 00:24:28.580
Well if it makes you feel any better,

00:24:28.580 --> 00:24:31.250
I also suffered an injury.

00:24:31.250 --> 00:24:32.083
Oh, good.

00:24:32.083 --> 00:24:34.107
Yeah, I really did.

00:24:34.107 --> 00:24:37.720
You know, I tried to psych myself up

00:24:37.720 --> 00:24:39.230
to low expectations,

00:24:39.230 --> 00:24:40.530
I was like...

00:24:40.530 --> 00:24:42.815
Psych yourself up for low expectations.

00:24:42.815 --> 00:24:43.813
Yeah, for the same reason,

00:24:43.813 --> 00:24:47.100
because I always have an
idea of what the perfect

00:24:47.100 --> 00:24:50.650
anything is, and so there's this standard

00:24:50.650 --> 00:24:52.439
that I'm constantly trying to meet,

00:24:52.439 --> 00:24:57.439
and bring my family along
to meet that same standard,

00:24:57.440 --> 00:25:00.950
so I was just telling myself...

00:25:00.950 --> 00:25:02.550
Which severely complicates it,

00:25:02.550 --> 00:25:04.931
when other people, you're
expecting other people,

00:25:04.931 --> 00:25:06.738
it's even worse.

00:25:06.738 --> 00:25:09.420
You know what? This is very
limited, we can't go out,

00:25:09.420 --> 00:25:11.760
we can't make a lot of
plans, 'cause we're either

00:25:11.760 --> 00:25:13.470
gonna be at home, we're
gonna order takeout,

00:25:13.470 --> 00:25:15.170
and we're gonna go to the beach,

00:25:15.170 --> 00:25:17.860
and I'm not gonna put any timetable,

00:25:17.860 --> 00:25:20.370
or we're not gonna make any big plans

00:25:20.370 --> 00:25:23.050
that require being
anywhere at a certain time,

00:25:23.050 --> 00:25:24.380
or anything like that,

00:25:24.380 --> 00:25:27.550
and it was the most laid back
vacation I've ever been on

00:25:27.550 --> 00:25:28.610
for that reason.

00:25:28.610 --> 00:25:30.890
I didn't even make the kids
get up at a certain time,

00:25:30.890 --> 00:25:32.220
oh, we gotta get on the beach,

00:25:32.220 --> 00:25:34.967
we gotta get parking space,
or we're gonna be so far away

00:25:34.967 --> 00:25:37.440
I'm gonna have to tote
everything for everybody,

00:25:37.440 --> 00:25:39.100
I'm gonna have to make
two trips, three trips,

00:25:39.100 --> 00:25:42.080
all the stuff I get worked up about.

00:25:42.080 --> 00:25:46.472
You know, it wasn't an
issue, there was parking.

00:25:46.472 --> 00:25:47.520
Yeah.

00:25:47.520 --> 00:25:50.140
So it was definitely the
most laid back vacation,

00:25:50.140 --> 00:25:54.156
I think, and having
those lower expectations

00:25:54.156 --> 00:25:58.800
really helped bring me
to what I said, a seven,

00:25:58.800 --> 00:26:00.280
but I did have an injury.

00:26:00.280 --> 00:26:05.280
I mean, I was like, I'm gonna
eat all the foods I wanna eat,

