01:07:36.170 --> 01:07:38.130
So other people have tried to intervene.

01:07:38.130 --> 01:07:40.110
Multiple people, his friends,

01:07:40.110 --> 01:07:41.910
and even a Russian lady.

01:07:41.910 --> 01:07:43.060
Okay, that helps the
producers' case a little bit.

01:07:43.060 --> 01:07:46.980
A Russian lady who was on
the services that he met

01:07:46.980 --> 01:07:50.200
at one time is telling
him that this is a scam

01:07:50.200 --> 01:07:51.691
and he meets her when he goes over there.

01:07:51.691 --> 01:07:52.524
Oh.

01:07:52.524 --> 01:07:54.250
And she since got
married to somebody else,

01:07:54.250 --> 01:07:55.476
and she's out of the game now,

01:07:55.476 --> 01:07:58.130
but so he goes back over
there for a fourth time,

01:07:58.130 --> 01:07:59.530
of course she doesn't show up.

01:07:59.530 --> 01:08:02.314
He comes back home, and then, you know,

01:08:02.314 --> 01:08:04.870
a couple hours later,
I'm still in the bed,

01:08:04.870 --> 01:08:06.030
I'm still watching this,

01:08:06.030 --> 01:08:08.222
he's going back again.

01:08:08.222 --> 01:08:10.470
Why are you doing,

01:08:10.470 --> 01:08:13.866
I can't believe you're watching this.

01:08:13.866 --> 01:08:16.470
I'm also following like five other couples

01:08:16.470 --> 01:08:17.303
at the same time,

01:08:17.303 --> 01:08:19.358
but I just, this one in particular,

01:08:19.358 --> 01:08:22.605
I was like, I just
don't, how is it possible

01:08:22.605 --> 01:08:26.075
that he's going there for the fifth time?

01:08:26.075 --> 01:08:29.970
And then he's like, okay,
she's supposed to be there

01:08:29.970 --> 01:08:32.233
at 11 o'clock, he's
still never talked to her

01:08:32.233 --> 01:08:33.986
through anything but the chat.

01:08:33.986 --> 01:08:34.985
Yup.

01:08:34.985 --> 01:08:36.331
And this very distinct blonde woman.

01:08:36.331 --> 01:08:40.400
Spoiler alert, don't listen
to what I'm about to say

01:08:40.400 --> 01:08:42.193
if you want to enjoy this yourself.

01:08:43.930 --> 01:08:45.164
She's there.

01:08:45.164 --> 01:08:45.997
What?

01:08:45.997 --> 01:08:48.055
The woman from the pictures shows up

01:08:48.055 --> 01:08:50.380
and hugs him.

01:08:50.380 --> 01:08:54.304
And I'm just like, having
invested so much time into this,

01:08:54.304 --> 01:08:57.857
and feeling so worthless,
it was like another hit.

01:08:57.857 --> 01:08:59.191
What?

01:08:59.191 --> 01:09:01.270
It was all of a sudden like
ah, this was all worth it.

01:09:01.270 --> 01:09:04.360
What, but hold on, she was an actress?

01:09:04.360 --> 01:09:05.220
No.

01:09:05.220 --> 01:09:06.110
They just brought in.

01:09:06.110 --> 01:09:07.260
So many things were going through my mind,

01:09:07.260 --> 01:09:09.060
I was like, did the
TLC producers like find

01:09:09.060 --> 01:09:10.380
this woman from the pictures and say, hey,

01:09:10.380 --> 01:09:12.636
will you act like it
was you this whole time?

01:09:12.636 --> 01:09:13.640
Yeah, this will make his day.

01:09:13.640 --> 01:09:15.250
It was her.

01:09:15.250 --> 01:09:19.850
But when they interviewed
her, it was very clear

01:09:19.850 --> 01:09:21.854
that she was continuing to carry on,

01:09:21.854 --> 01:09:25.810
she wants the money, she
wants the gifts from him,

01:09:25.810 --> 01:09:30.810
and it seems that she wants
the ability to come to the US.

01:09:31.060 --> 01:09:33.510
I think, at this point,
where I stopped watching

01:09:33.510 --> 01:09:35.260
the show was the tell all,

01:09:35.260 --> 01:09:36.660
which was like during COVID,

01:09:36.660 --> 01:09:38.270
where they're all on video chat.

01:09:38.270 --> 01:09:39.103
Oh wow.

01:09:39.103 --> 01:09:41.638
So like after the after the 90 Days,

01:09:41.638 --> 01:09:44.168
she didn't even show up for that.

01:09:44.168 --> 01:09:46.600
And he was like, I haven't
spoken to her in six days,

01:09:46.600 --> 01:09:47.433
I think the engagement,

01:09:47.433 --> 01:09:48.523
they got engaged.

01:09:49.370 --> 01:09:51.052
They got engaged?

01:09:51.052 --> 01:09:52.656
And I was just like...

01:09:52.656 --> 01:09:57.480
So she's also maybe an addict too.

01:09:57.480 --> 01:09:59.600
Like whatever he's giving her.

01:09:59.600 --> 01:10:00.970
She's addicted to money, man.

01:10:00.970 --> 01:10:01.803
Okay.

01:10:01.803 --> 01:10:05.958
But it was, I had to follow this story.

01:10:05.958 --> 01:10:07.714
And that becomes a 90 Day Fiance episode?

01:10:07.714 --> 01:10:09.404
I guess.

01:10:09.404 --> 01:10:13.380
But it was so, like I don't
know what the moral of it is,

01:10:13.380 --> 01:10:14.890
I mean, for me...

01:10:14.890 --> 01:10:16.120
It's tough.

01:10:16.120 --> 01:10:18.800
For me it's just like
I can't let this happen

01:10:18.800 --> 01:10:20.520
unless I'm on vacation, right?

01:10:20.520 --> 01:10:23.528
I feel worthless, I hate
myself for doing this,

01:10:23.528 --> 01:10:26.580
I don't know why I'm so
invested in finding out

01:10:26.580 --> 01:10:27.920
if this woman's real.

01:10:27.920 --> 01:10:30.070
I don't know what's gonna
happen with Ed and Rose,

01:10:30.070 --> 01:10:32.450
I mean, Ed told Rose that
she needed to shave her legs

01:10:32.450 --> 01:10:34.300
and that she had bad
breath, and it's like,

01:10:34.300 --> 01:10:36.261
I don't like the way
that he told her that.

01:10:36.261 --> 01:10:40.450
But how's she gonna
respond, and then like oh,

01:10:40.450 --> 01:10:43.760
is what's her name gonna
find out that Williams is not

01:10:43.760 --> 01:10:46.396
a real dude, that she's being catfished?

01:10:46.396 --> 01:10:50.263
Like you find yourself
so invested in this.

01:10:51.676 --> 01:10:54.950
Moral of the story for
David though, I think, is

01:10:54.950 --> 01:10:56.930
if you have a delusion, just follow it

01:10:56.930 --> 01:10:58.690
to the end of the yellow brick road.

01:10:58.690 --> 01:10:59.523
You're probably right.

01:10:59.523 --> 01:11:00.929
It may come true.

01:11:00.929 --> 01:11:04.720
Now listen, I'm not shutting this down,

01:11:04.720 --> 01:11:05.860
cause I got...

01:11:05.860 --> 01:11:07.500
Questions.

01:11:07.500 --> 01:11:08.333
I'm flooded.

01:11:08.333 --> 01:11:09.505
You should just watch it.

01:11:09.505 --> 01:11:11.410
I'm flooded with memories
associated with this, so.

01:11:11.410 --> 01:11:14.025
Hold on, you've been
talking to a Ukrainian woman

01:11:14.025 --> 01:11:15.298
?

01:11:15.298 --> 01:11:16.655
I don't care if this goes,

01:11:16.655 --> 01:11:18.646
you know what, this may be a part two.

01:11:18.646 --> 01:11:20.067
Don't .

01:11:21.140 --> 01:11:22.760
Let's just blow it open.

01:11:22.760 --> 01:11:25.925
Every time you get so invested
in a freaking trash show

01:11:25.925 --> 01:11:27.610
it becomes an episode.

01:11:27.610 --> 01:11:29.550
I think I need my own podcast
where I just talk about

01:11:29.550 --> 01:11:31.510
reality TV, can we do that?

01:11:31.510 --> 01:11:33.144
Well, am I not invited?

01:11:33.144 --> 01:11:34.676
I mean...

01:11:34.676 --> 01:11:36.850
Somebody's gotta tell
you you have a problem

01:11:36.850 --> 01:11:39.210
and that you just can't give in to this.

01:11:39.210 --> 01:11:42.130
See, you need to take a breath.

01:11:42.130 --> 01:11:43.860
No, but if I can make money off of it,

01:11:43.860 --> 01:11:45.770
then I start to feel
like I'm worth something.

01:11:45.770 --> 01:11:47.920
Like if I could take my addiction

01:11:47.920 --> 01:11:49.842
to TLC and other things like it

01:11:49.842 --> 01:11:54.530
and turn it into a paying project,

01:11:54.530 --> 01:11:56.830
then I'll say, oh this, okay, that's good,

01:11:56.830 --> 01:11:57.663
this makes sense.

01:11:57.663 --> 01:11:59.080
It validates your addiction.

01:11:59.080 --> 01:12:00.267
Spending seven hours,

01:12:00.267 --> 01:12:04.050
I mean this is like
those people who sit down

01:12:04.050 --> 01:12:05.922
and watch all three of Lord of the Rings

01:12:05.922 --> 01:12:08.980
back to back to back, which,
I'm just not that kind

01:12:08.980 --> 01:12:09.813
of person.

01:12:09.813 --> 01:12:10.880
I cannot do that.

01:12:10.880 --> 01:12:12.500
But it's not, because...

01:12:12.500 --> 01:12:13.626
It's not Lord of the Rings.

01:12:13.626 --> 01:12:15.200
Yeah, it's a...

01:12:15.200 --> 01:12:16.580
It's far from it.

01:12:16.580 --> 01:12:21.580
It's real people that
have been just marionetted

01:12:21.820 --> 01:12:26.820
through producing and editing
for you to feel sorry for them

01:12:27.540 --> 01:12:28.857
or feel better about yourself,

01:12:28.857 --> 01:12:32.050
all of this psychology
it could be troubling.

01:12:32.050 --> 01:12:37.050
But it does remind me
when we started producing

01:12:37.280 --> 01:12:38.310
Commercial Kings.

01:12:38.310 --> 01:12:39.625
So we made the pilot.

01:12:39.625 --> 01:12:40.458
Yeah.

01:12:40.458 --> 01:12:43.210
With Revelly, we worked
with Todd, who brought us in

01:12:43.210 --> 01:12:46.568
and produced that and we had a producer

01:12:46.568 --> 01:12:49.029
who worked on Survivor actually,

01:12:49.029 --> 01:12:53.233
shoot, his name is on
the tip of my tongue.

01:12:54.173 --> 01:12:55.890
Fernando.

01:12:55.890 --> 01:12:56.723
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:12:56.723 --> 01:12:59.198
Fernando was the one who was,

01:12:59.198 --> 01:13:02.261
we were filming the pilot
episode in the mountains of

01:13:02.261 --> 01:13:04.540
Asheville, North Carolina,

01:13:04.540 --> 01:13:08.173
and with Heavy Hill the Trash Man,

01:13:08.173 --> 01:13:10.110
the garbage collector.

01:13:10.110 --> 01:13:11.158
Yeah.

01:13:11.158 --> 01:13:12.680
And then we had some downtime

01:13:12.680 --> 01:13:14.447
and we hadn't talked
about it ahead of time

01:13:14.447 --> 01:13:16.463
and all of a sudden, Fernando's like,

01:13:16.463 --> 01:13:21.463
we wanna set up some OTF interviews.

01:13:21.607 --> 01:13:22.610
We were like OTF?

01:13:22.610 --> 01:13:24.410
On the fly interviews.

01:13:24.410 --> 01:13:28.020
It's like you know in like
reality competition shows

01:13:28.020 --> 01:13:30.150
and stuff like that they
have confession cams

01:13:30.150 --> 01:13:31.790
or they'll be talking to a producer.

01:13:31.790 --> 01:13:32.920
And we hadn't thought about this at all.

01:13:32.920 --> 01:13:34.250
Hadn't thought about it at all

01:13:34.250 --> 01:13:36.510
and he was like it may
not be part of the show,

01:13:36.510 --> 01:13:37.910
but let's just do it.

01:13:37.910 --> 01:13:40.874
And then we made a decision

01:13:40.874 --> 01:13:43.178
he wanted us to do them individually,

01:13:43.178 --> 01:13:46.530
we didn't feel good
about that, I remember.

01:13:46.530 --> 01:13:47.480
But we did it.

01:13:47.480 --> 01:13:52.480
I remember he set up a shot
of me standing in front of

01:13:52.606 --> 01:13:55.900
Heavy Hill's shed, in his backyard,

01:13:55.900 --> 01:13:57.420
where he had his pet mule back there.

01:13:57.420 --> 01:13:58.513
Yeah, I remember this.

01:13:58.513 --> 01:14:01.400
Then you had a little downtime
while he interviewed me.

01:14:01.400 --> 01:14:03.290
I remember when he interviewed
you I was like watching,

01:14:03.290 --> 01:14:04.543
I was like, I think he
interviewed you first.

01:14:04.543 --> 01:14:06.476
I was like how's this gonna go?

01:14:06.476 --> 01:14:10.403
And here we were, we
like to be in control.

01:14:10.403 --> 01:14:15.403
It was our show, we were
producers on the show too.

01:14:15.454 --> 01:14:17.630
Yeah, executive producers.

01:14:17.630 --> 01:14:18.463
Executive producers,

01:14:18.463 --> 01:14:20.690
and we were producing the
commercial within the show,

01:14:20.690 --> 01:14:23.450
so it's like we had
our hands in all of it.

01:14:23.450 --> 01:14:24.623
Yeah.

01:14:24.623 --> 01:14:27.900
And it felt a little weird

01:14:27.900 --> 01:14:30.254
being interviewed by Fernando, who like,

01:14:30.254 --> 01:14:33.330
in one sense worked for us,

01:14:33.330 --> 01:14:34.808
but then he was interviewing us,

01:14:34.808 --> 01:14:37.900
documenting the process of
us making these commercials,

01:14:37.900 --> 01:14:40.440
so like he would throw things at us

01:14:40.440 --> 01:14:41.681
and we would talk about it,

01:14:41.681 --> 01:14:42.514
and then they go,

01:14:42.514 --> 01:14:45.652
and then that ended up
being cut into the episode.

01:14:45.652 --> 01:14:47.330
But then when we went to,

01:14:47.330 --> 01:14:50.260
all of that was a tangent by the way,

01:14:50.260 --> 01:14:51.433
Oh, you're getting somewhere.

01:14:51.433 --> 01:14:53.890
Well I guess we became,

01:14:53.890 --> 01:14:56.260
that was where I started to feel like

01:14:56.260 --> 01:14:57.587
we were actually...

01:14:57.587 --> 01:14:58.420
Employed?

01:14:58.420 --> 01:15:01.083
No, we were in a reality television show.

01:15:02.070 --> 01:15:04.220
Commercial Kings was
the show documenting us

01:15:04.220 --> 01:15:06.930
making a commercial, but we
never thought of it that way.

01:15:06.930 --> 01:15:08.867
We thought of it as we
were producing a show

01:15:08.867 --> 01:15:11.588
that shows how we make the commercials.

01:15:11.588 --> 01:15:15.580
But what Fernando tried to
achieve was a level of detachment

01:15:15.580 --> 01:15:18.660
from how we were gonna be presented.

01:15:18.660 --> 01:15:20.550
And what we're processing
at the same time.

01:15:20.550 --> 01:15:24.359
And let out process and
and our point of view

01:15:24.359 --> 01:15:26.780
not just become editorial

01:15:26.780 --> 01:15:28.550
but become something
that happened on screen.

01:15:28.550 --> 01:15:30.470
And it's difficult when the
people that you're doing

01:15:30.470 --> 01:15:32.180
that with are really self aware.

01:15:32.180 --> 01:15:33.480
And also producing the show.

01:15:33.480 --> 01:15:35.493
Yeah, meaning us, we're pretty self aware.

01:15:35.493 --> 01:15:37.090
We're pretty good at separating ourselves.

01:15:37.090 --> 01:15:38.890
So it's like when he'd ask us a question,

01:15:38.890 --> 01:15:40.365
half the time we were thinking,

01:15:40.365 --> 01:15:43.410
what is the best way
to answer this question

01:15:43.410 --> 01:15:45.610
to be entertaining but
also connect the dots

01:15:45.610 --> 01:15:48.238
so that in the edit room
we can tell the best story,

01:15:48.238 --> 01:15:49.239
and that...

01:15:49.239 --> 01:15:51.070
We would be way better at that now

01:15:51.070 --> 01:15:52.310
than we were in 2011.

01:15:52.310 --> 01:15:53.640
Oh yeah, we weren't good at it.

01:15:53.640 --> 01:15:54.473
No, no.

01:15:54.473 --> 01:15:57.300
But if we were to just let
go and trusted Fernando

01:15:57.300 --> 01:15:59.350
and just answered his questions,

01:15:59.350 --> 01:16:01.460
Which we would do now.
Which we would do now.

01:16:01.460 --> 01:16:03.420
Where we understand how to be ourselves.

01:16:03.420 --> 01:16:04.480
Yes.

01:16:04.480 --> 01:16:06.300
A lot more than we did in the early days.

01:16:06.300 --> 01:16:07.133
Like right now.

01:16:07.133 --> 01:16:07.966
Yeah.

01:16:08.880 --> 01:16:10.280
There's so many times
I wish we could go back

01:16:10.280 --> 01:16:11.873
and do Commercial Kings again.

01:16:11.873 --> 01:16:14.160
And I think that was a part of it.

01:16:14.160 --> 01:16:16.850
It stuck in our crawl that
like we were doing these

01:16:16.850 --> 01:16:18.520
on the fly interviews.

01:16:18.520 --> 01:16:19.353
And that's the part of the
show I don't like watching,

01:16:19.353 --> 01:16:21.051
I don't like watching those interviews.

01:16:21.051 --> 01:16:22.700
In series though,

01:16:22.700 --> 01:16:24.760
and this is what I was
originally getting to,

01:16:24.760 --> 01:16:27.895
so it wasn't a tangent, a
continuation of my though.

01:16:27.895 --> 01:16:30.630
In series, we worked with a
different production company,

01:16:30.630 --> 01:16:32.271
we worked with Joke Productions.

01:16:32.271 --> 01:16:37.271
Revelly, the company that
funded the show and sold it

01:16:38.262 --> 01:16:40.533
and produced the pilot,

01:16:40.533 --> 01:16:42.920
they basically said we need
to bring in somebody else

01:16:42.920 --> 01:16:44.820
who does this day in and day out.

01:16:44.820 --> 01:16:45.771
Yeah.

01:16:45.771 --> 01:16:47.820
Who can do it on a tighter budget.

01:16:47.820 --> 01:16:48.745
Yeah.

01:16:48.745 --> 01:16:52.823
Joke Productions was Joke and Biagio,

01:16:52.823 --> 01:16:57.823
they were a married couple,
and Joke is her name.

01:16:57.848 --> 01:17:00.936
For some reason she's
like Belgian or something.

01:17:00.936 --> 01:17:01.960
Yeah.

01:17:01.960 --> 01:17:05.920
And so Joke doesn't mean
funny ha ha over there.

01:17:05.920 --> 01:17:07.890
But it works well, translates well.

01:17:07.890 --> 01:17:09.632
I made all that up, I
actually don't know why

01:17:09.632 --> 01:17:11.502
they called her Joke.

01:17:11.502 --> 01:17:12.790
That's her name.

01:17:12.790 --> 01:17:13.623
Was that right?

01:17:13.623 --> 01:17:15.073
Yeah.

01:17:15.073 --> 01:17:16.490
It did mean funny ha ha in Belgium?

01:17:16.490 --> 01:17:18.450
I don't think so, I
think it's just a name.

01:17:18.450 --> 01:17:20.093
Okay, maybe I wasn't joking.

01:17:20.093 --> 01:17:23.850
Sometimes I say things just
because they might be cool

01:17:23.850 --> 01:17:26.500
to say, and then I realize
I'm accessing a memory

01:17:26.500 --> 01:17:27.720
that I didn't know I had.

01:17:27.720 --> 01:17:29.370
Oh, well that's part of life.

01:17:29.370 --> 01:17:32.051
I remember the first
episode we shot with them

01:17:32.051 --> 01:17:35.660
was Make me a Pro Wrestler.

01:17:35.660 --> 01:17:37.380
That was the name of the
business we were doing

01:17:37.380 --> 01:17:38.560
the commercial for.

01:17:38.560 --> 01:17:39.830
We aired em all out of order.

01:17:39.830 --> 01:17:42.710
The Heavy Hill pilot episode
aired somewhere in the middle.

01:17:42.710 --> 01:17:45.190
The Make me a Pro
Wrestler didn't turn out,

01:17:45.190 --> 01:17:48.020
it was a dynamic commercial,

01:17:48.020 --> 01:17:49.840
it had all that action,
but it didn't have a hook

01:17:49.840 --> 01:17:51.192
and it wasn't .

01:17:51.192 --> 01:17:52.025
It didn't come together.

01:17:52.025 --> 01:17:53.050
But we learnt how to be wrestlers

01:17:53.050 --> 01:17:54.720
and you freaking, with
your back and everything,

01:17:54.720 --> 01:17:55.610
suplexed me.

01:17:55.610 --> 01:17:57.670
And it hurt my back, by the way.

01:17:57.670 --> 01:17:58.625
Yeah it did.

01:17:58.625 --> 01:18:00.550
But we tried to get the guy

01:18:00.550 --> 01:18:04.070
who was called the hobo, right?

01:18:04.070 --> 01:18:07.900
Yeah, right, his wrestling
persona was the hobo,

01:18:07.900 --> 01:18:09.540
we interviewed them all

01:18:09.540 --> 01:18:11.117
and we wanted to...

01:18:11.117 --> 01:18:12.719
